WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.402
-Our next guest is a talented
actress and comedian you know

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.805
from shows like "Shrill"
and "I Think You Should Leave"

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.907
as well as the film
"Together Together."

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.776
You can see her next
in "The Lost City,"

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.945
which is in theaters March 25th.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.847
Let's take a look.
-This is Allison.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:17.117
She is our new social-media
manager, and she's going to be

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.352
helping us target
that younger demographic,

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.888
meaning women in their 30s
who wish they were in their 20s.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.723
-Hey, what's up?

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:24.991
I took over your social.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:29.161
So this morning you tweeted
"Where my ladies at?

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:31.964
Meet me at Ballroom G
at 5:00 p.m.

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:33.799
#Shawnmendes.

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:36.669
#Gagging to meet you all."

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:40.173
-Please welcome to the show
Patti Harrison, everybody!

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.241
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:49.449 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:56.623 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.290
Welcome to the show, Patti.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.693
-Thank you.
-This is a very big film.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.695
Sandra Bullock,
Daniel Radcliffe,

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.064
Brad Pitt, Channing Tatum.
-Yeah.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.966
-Filmed in
the Dominican Republic.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.235
-Randy.
-Randy?

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.803
Who's Randy?
-The goat.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:13.205
-The goat? There's a goat.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:15.541
Had you worked with
a goat before?

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:18.043
-In almost every project
I've taken on.

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:19.478
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.478 --> 00:01:20.780
-There's been a goat.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.815
-That's sort of on your rider.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:23.916
The thing you need.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.851
-Yeah. Inclusion rider.

00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:29.689
That's what Frances meant when
she stood up and demanded that.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:32.324
-She said, "Every film should
have at least one goat."

00:01:32.324 --> 00:01:36.195
I can imagine some goats are
easier to work with than others.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:37.497
How was Randy?

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.732
-Randy was --
[ Sighs ]

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:43.803
I feel like, you know, I just
want to be a more honest person,

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.471
especially in, like,
today's climate.

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:48.741
I feel like I don't want --
I don't think people

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.843
have the bandwidth
for fakeness anymore.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.278
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:55.715
That being said, I don't know
if Randy's handler is listening.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.751
I don't know if Randy's handler
will be offended by the fact

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.153
that I don't think Randy's name
is actually Randy.

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:03.656
That's the character's name.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.791
I didn't even take the time
to learn the actor's name,

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:07.526
which is, like, you know,

00:02:07.526 --> 00:02:10.763
high-spectrum narcissism
kind of crap.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:14.200
-That is a little lousy that you
didn't go out of your way to --

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.035
-Well, Randy didn't have
a lot of credits.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.970
And, like, I was like...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.472
-So it's not about it
being a goat versus a human.

00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:23.609
It was just that as an actor,
he hadn't done a lot.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:26.312
-Yeah. It was like, could I
either corner Sandra Bullock

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.381
and try to network with her
until she dies,

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.816
or should I do that to Randy?

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.484
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.519
Yeah, the choice there
is obvious.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.288
-And when I say
"until she dies,"

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.922
I mean I network her to death.

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:38.424
[ Laughter ]
I ask her if she wants --

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:41.761
-So within a matter of days,
we might be mourning?

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.230
-Yeah, I'm asking her
if she wants to get coffee

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.965
so I can pick her brain
about the biz

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.933
for about four or five days.
-Is that your dream,

00:02:47.933 --> 00:02:50.102
to reach the point where someone
comes up to you and says,

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:52.538
"I'd love to get coffee and pick
your brain about the business"?

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:56.675
-I mean, I've had people
do that in, like,

00:02:56.675 --> 00:02:59.011
a more dark and disturbing way.

00:02:59.011 --> 00:03:00.813
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.649
-Yeah. On dating apps sometimes.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:08.421
I live in L.A., and it's a very
specific place to live

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:13.893
because everybody there,
there's not a lot of, I think --

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.229
and I'm generalizing the city,
again.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.730
You know, sorry, Randy,
sorry, the city of L.A.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:23.403
But a lot of people are actors
or aspiring to do so.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:26.171
-Yeah.
-So if they recognize me

00:03:26.171 --> 00:03:27.806
in any capacity,
which it's like,

00:03:27.806 --> 00:03:29.042
I don't think
I'm a famous person,

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.843
but in L.A., a lot of people

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.478
will just have
this hyperawareness.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:36.982
-Mm-hmm.
-So I'm transgender and I've had

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:41.453
guys on dating apps be like,
you know,

00:03:41.453 --> 00:03:43.056
"I've never dated a trans woman

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:45.157
and I'm not romantically
attracted to trans women,

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:46.392
but I think you're really funny

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.294
and I'd like to pick your brain
about comedy."

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.495
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.495 --> 00:03:54.367
Which is, like, so horny.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.335
-What a turn-on.

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:57.336
-It's really good.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.336 --> 00:03:58.604
I'm sorry.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:03:59.672
There's so many boners
in the audience right now.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.707
-Every point of the checklist
there

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:05.711
of like, how to attract --

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:07.280
-I actually like it now.
I didn't at first.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.415
That's all to say
it's a positive thing.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.017
It used to be a negative thing
for me,

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.552
but that's actually what
I'm attracted to now,

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:16.022
so keep doing it.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:18.223
-You were profiled in
"The New Yorker."

00:04:18.223 --> 00:04:20.560
I mean, obviously, it's
a very esteemed magazine.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.961
Did it feel like
a career achievement

00:04:22.961 --> 00:04:26.798
to be written about
in "The New Yorker"?

00:04:26.798 --> 00:04:28.668
-I mean, it felt cool.

00:04:30.302 --> 00:04:33.305
As someone who doesn't
read at all and hasn't --

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:35.040
[ Laughter ]
I can read.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.875
[ Laughter ]
I'm not one of those people

00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:38.878
that thinks it's funny
to be illiterate

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.879
'cause I think
that's a hard life to live.

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:42.682
No, don't laugh.
It's a really hard life to live.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.150
-Mm-hmm.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.318
-But I don't read.

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:47.720
I can and I choose not to.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.322
-I feel like that's
a very powerful stance

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:51.724
that not a lot of people take.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.225
Like, to go through
all the work of learning

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:55.128
how to do it and then like,
"No."

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:57.964
[ Laughter ]
-Well, it felt really -- Yeah.

00:04:57.964 --> 00:05:01.200
I try and inspire as many people
not to read as possible.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.668
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:06.305
I say if you go to someone's
house you're on a date with

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:08.007
and you see that
they have books, run.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.475
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:12.478
So, a lot of people sometimes,
I think, will posture to show

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.113
how learned they are by saying

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.548
they subscribe to
"The New Yorker."

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.517
Is it safe to say you don't
subscribe to "The New Yorker"?

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:21.554
